@startuml "Facade - Notification - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Facade — five subsystems, and what the client carries


package "problem" {
  class ClientBefore as "Client" {
    - email : EmailService
    - sms : SMSService
    - slack : SlackService
    - push : PushNotificationService
    - logger : NotificationLogger
  }
}

package "solution" {
  class ClientAfter as "Client" {
    - notifications : NotificationFacade
  }
  class NotificationFacade <<Facade>> {
    + notify(user, title, body)
    + notify(user, channels, title, body)
  }
  class EmailService
  class SMSService
  class SlackService
  class PushNotificationService
  class NotificationLogger

  ClientAfter --> NotificationFacade
  NotificationFacade ..> EmailService
  NotificationFacade ..> SMSService
  NotificationFacade ..> SlackService
  NotificationFacade ..> PushNotificationService
  NotificationFacade ..> NotificationLogger
}

note bottom of ClientBefore
  <b>Five</b> dependencies for one
  responsibility — in every class
  that sends a notification.

  And the rules (do-not-disturb,
  the 160-character SMS limit) are
  re-typed in each of them.
end note

note bottom of ClientAfter
  <b>One.</b> And the rules live in the
  facade, so no client can forget
  them.
end note

@enduml
